WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.270
Some monks in India sweep the path
in front of them as they walk.

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.710
They are Jains.

3
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.150
They hope not to crush
even the tiniest creature.

4
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.940
This is ahimsa: not
harming any living being,

5
00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.610
in thought, word or deed.

6
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.220
Many Hindus, too, avoid
meat for the same reason.

7
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:23.340
So is it possible to live
without harming anything at all?

8
00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:27.350
In this mission, you'll see how
Hindu texts teach non-violence,

9
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.950
and how Hindus apply it to animals.

10
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.930
Then you'll weigh up whether ahimsa is a
realistic standard in the modern world.

11
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.920
Your mission: find out what
ahimsa really asks of a person.
